Z||000021||sluppy123||02-21-2000||12:25 PM||||This is the best pic I have of the sub<P><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=247832&a=1876291&p=16542924&Sequence=0" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=247832&a=1876291&p=16542924&Sequence=0</A> <P>MM-The sub box fills the entire pass. foot well, so you do lose some leg room. the dimensions for the box are the same as the foot well. I started with carboard and duct-tape to get the right size and contours. then used fiberglass to cover the cardboard, added a 3/4" MDF front, cut the hole for the sub(I used a 8" but a 10" will fit), and carpeted it. <P><p>[This message has been edited by sluppy123 (edited 02-21-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000022||ounmongk||02-21-2000||12:49 PM||||I still think that the bass tubes on the floors, in front of the seats are the best way to go, you don't lose any leg room and with smaller speakers, you get more accurate bass hits. Just my opinion though. Anyone have any instructions or tips on how to go about this kind of install? ||||reg||1
Z||000023||SpeedPhreak||02-21-2000||01:04 PM||||kicker just came out w/a new square sub.  i dont know much about them but i do know that they are made for small boxes (like the next generation of the solobaric i guess) & make much more noise/bass for the space than conventional round speakers.||||reg||1
Z||000024||1FST2M6||02-21-2000||01:30 PM||||I've already paid for mine! (3 actually) from Sound Sensations in marietta, Ga. The new L7s are SWEET. No idea what they sound like but since they have about 20% more surface area than the ones i have now they have got to just SLAM!.. and Kicker doesn't let crap out of their facilitys! I have 2-10"s and a 12" comming.. One for the Fiero, One for the Alfa and the 12 for the girlfriends Saturn!  What kind of amp is everyone running? any one with a decent Cap install? In a fiero.. of course. I had to just bolt the 2 I'm running to the floor.. Kinda cheezy looking! any other ideas? oh their $189 (10") and $229 (12")  <A HREF="http://www.kicker.com" TARGET=_blank>www.kicker.com</A>  I'll be sure to post a pic of the new install!<p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 02-21-2000).]||||reg||1
