Z||000027||william_thorniii||02-21-2000||06:30 PM||||Doughboy,<P>A Corbeau is a brand of racing seat.  2M6 has pictures up in the General Forum of it.  I think that he put them up about 1-2 weeks ago. <P>Everyone,<P>I am not going to slam the square sub idea... but I can tell you that physically speaking it doesn't make sense.  What I mean is that sound travel's in waves that are in the form of circles starting from their originating point.  The question I have is what will it do to the doppler effect?  It is the same argument as 4x10 vs 4" round and 6X9 vs. 6" round.  The camp that do not care about sound quality usually go for more cone since more cone = more air movement = more bass.  The stereophiles go for round = less distortion = more accurate representation of music.  I am obviously a member of the stereophile camp.  This information is not opinion and therefore, I am not wrong and I don't care what company produces them they cannot change the laws of physics.  They might be able to make a square sub sound good, but it is physically impossible that it will sound as good as an equivalent round.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||13
